.TH BALROGG 1 "@BLR_DATE@" "balrogg @PACKAGE_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
balrogg \- lossless Ogg Vorbis and Ogg Opus recompressor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B balrogg
.RB [ \-1 .. \-20 ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.B e
.I input output
.br
.B balrogg
.RB [ \-p ]
.B d
.I input output
.br
.B balrogg
.RB [ \-1 .. \-20 ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-j
.IR N ]
.B \-b
.BR e | d
.IR file ...
.br
.B balrogg
.BR \-h | \-v
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B balrogg
losslessly recompresses Ogg Vorbis and Opus files, MP3 files (MPEG-1, 2
and 2.5 Layer III), and MOD modules (ProTracker and compatible 31-sample
modules, and 15-sample Soundtracker modules). Expanding an archive restores the
original bytes.
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.B e
Compress
.I input
to
.IR output .
Files that cannot be reproduced exactly are refused.
.TP
.B d
Expand the archive
.I input
to
.IR output .
The archive stores the length and CRC-32C of the original file; a decoded file
that does not match them is refused and removed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-1 " .. " \-20
Effort.
.B \-8
is the default. Each level is (ideally) no faster than the one below it and gives
archives no larger on any class of file.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-progress
Show encoding and decoding progress bars on stderr. Off by default.
.TP
.B \-\-progress-lines
Write progress checkpoints as separate lines, suitable for log files.
.TP
.B \-\-no-mmap
Use heap memory for model arenas and buffered file I/O instead of memory
mappings.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-batch
Every remaining argument is an input. Encoding writes
.IR file .blr
beside each input and decoding strips the suffix, or appends
.B .out
when there is none. Files run in separate processes within CPU and memory
limits. Larger inputs start first. Remaining files continue after a refusal.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs = \fIN\fR
Run
.I N
files at once instead of measuring the machine.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version, build host, and source libopus release.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Malformed, unsupported, or unrecognized input, or a decoded file that fails
its checksum. In batch mode, at least one
file was refused and no higher status occurred.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
A file could not be opened, read or written.
.TP
.B 4
Internal error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BLR_MEMCAP
Per-process memory cap in MiB. The default is 2048. A value of 0 disables it.
Sanitizer builds omit the cap.
.TP
.B BLR_REGION
A value of 0 takes blocks of 1 KiB to 4 MiB from the C library, not from the
never-unmapped region that serves them otherwise.
.B \-\-no\-mmap
does the same.
.TP
.B BLR_SIMD
Select the context-mixer kernel on x86.
.B scalar
forces the portable kernel and the portable CRC-32C;
.B sse2
and
.B avx2
require the requested kernel to be built and supported by the CPU.
AVX2 also requires OS support for saving XMM and YMM state.
The default prefers AVX2, then SSE2, then the scalar kernel.
.SH LIMITS
Input must be seekable, and so must the output of Ogg archives; MP3 and MOD
archives also decode to a pipe. MOD modules larger than 1 GiB are stored. An output that is not a regular file, such as a pipe or
.IR /dev/null ,
is checked as it is written: on a checksum mismatch the bytes already written
cannot be taken back, and only the exit status reports it.
.PP
Opus mode supports channel mapping families 0, 1 and 255, with packets
(including headers) up to 61,440 bytes.
Chained Opus and Vorbis files are supported. Their links share the adaptive
models. Vorbis floor type 0 and codebook lookup type 2 are unsupported.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
balrogg e track.ogg track.blr
balrogg d track.blr track.ogg
balrogg -5 -b e album/*.ogg
balrogg -b d album/*.blr
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Kamila Szewczyk <k@iczelia.net>
